<main>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="hero">
    <canvas id="net" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">LT 2010 · Spring Semester</p>
      <h1 class="reveal d1">Computer Skills for the Information Age</h1>
      <hr class="accent-rule reveal d1" />
      <p class="lede reveal d2">
        Computing, technology, and AI now shape how we learn, work, communicate, and decide.
        This course helps you become a thoughtful, capable, and ethical participant in a
        digital and AI-saturated world.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions reveal d3">
        <a class="btn" href="#schedule">See the week-by-week schedule<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <span class="startcue">Start here: Week 1 opens with a short AI &amp; digital-tool survey.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-strip reveal d4">
        <div class="cell"><div class="k">Prerequisites</div><div class="v">None</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="k">Designed for</div><div class="v">All backgrounds</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="k">Format</div><div class="v">Weekly units</div></div>
        <div class="cell"><div class="k">Assessed by</div><div class="v">3 assignments</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section id="overview">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">About the course</p>
        <h2>An orientation for a digital &amp; AI age</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This course helps you become a thoughtful, capable, and ethical participant in a world
          reshaped by computing, technology, and artificial intelligence. Over the term you'll use
          computing as a tool to <strong>work and create with data</strong>; learn effectively
          <strong>with and without AI</strong>; <strong>find and judge digital information</strong>;
          reason about the <strong>ethics of technology</strong>; and build a
          <strong>professional digital presence</strong> for your career.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's designed for students of every background — <strong>no prerequisites are required</strong>.
          Whether you arrive as a confident coder or have never opened a spreadsheet, you'll leave with
          practical skills and the judgment to use them well.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="how">
        <div class="h">
          <svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-learn"/></svg>
          <h3>A weekly rhythm</h3>
          <p>One topic and one discussion each week — a steady, predictable cadence you can plan around.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="h">
          <svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-compass"/></svg>
          <h3>Truly no prerequisites</h3>
          <p>Start wherever you are. Nothing here assumes prior coding or technical background.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="h">
          <svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-design"/></svg>
          <h3>Learn by doing</h3>
          <p>Three applied assignments turn ideas into things you've actually made and can show.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="h">
          <svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-break"/></svg>
          <h3>Breathing room</h3>
          <p>The final units span two weeks each so you can finish the term strong, not rushed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LEARNING GOALS -->
  <section id="goals">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you'll be able to do</p>
        <h2>Six skills you'll carry forward</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="goals">
        <article class="goal">
          <div class="badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-data"/></svg></div>
          <span class="tag">Data</span>
          <h3>Work with data</h3>
          <p>Use computing as a tool to gather, shape, and create with data — the raw material of modern work.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="goal">
          <div class="badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-learn"/></svg></div>
          <span class="tag">Learning</span>
          <h3>Learn how to learn</h3>
          <p>Build durable strategies for learning effectively, both with AI assistance and on your own.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="goal">
          <div class="badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-info"/></svg></div>
          <span class="tag">Information</span>
          <h3>Judge information</h3>
          <p>Find, evaluate, and decide what to trust across a noisy digital information landscape.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="goal">
          <div class="badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-ai"/></svg></div>
          <span class="tag">AI</span>
          <h3>Understand AI</h3>
          <p>Develop a working literacy for what AI can and can't do — and how to use it responsibly.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="goal">
          <div class="badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-ethics"/></svg></div>
          <span class="tag">Ethics</span>
          <h3>Reason about ethics</h3>
          <p>Think critically about the ethics, privacy, and power dynamics that technology sets in motion.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="goal">
          <div class="badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-identity"/></svg></div>
          <span class="tag">Identity</span>
          <h3>Present yourself</h3>
          <p>Create a professional digital presence and identity that serves your goals and career.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUTCOMES BAND -->
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="outcomes-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">In your words</p>
      <h2 id="outcomes-h">By the end, I can…</h2>
      <ul class="says">
        <li>find information and explain <em>why</em> I trust it.</li>
        <li>use AI as a tool — and know when <em>not</em> to.</li>
        <li>turn raw data into a story people actually understand.</li>
        <li>present a professional version of myself online.</li>
        <li>pick up a new tool without being intimidated by it.</li>
        <li>weigh the ethics of a technology before I adopt it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

