  <!-- OUR COMMITMENTS (ethics through-line) -->
  <section id="commitments">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work together</p>
        <h2>Our commitments to you</h2>
        <p class="sub">This is a course about technology and ethics, so we hold ourselves to the same standard we ask of the tools we study. These are the values behind every unit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="commit">
        <div class="cm">
          <div class="bd"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-heart"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Everyone belongs here</h3>
            <p>Whatever your background or comfort with technology, you have a place in this course. We design for beginners and build up together — no question is too basic.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cm">
          <div class="bd"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-lock"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Privacy by default</h3>
            <p>We'll be honest about what the tools we use collect, and we'll help you understand and control your own digital footprint rather than growing it carelessly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cm">
          <div class="bd"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-scale"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Ethics in every unit</h3>
            <p>For each technology we study, we ask not only "can we?" but "should we?" — weighing power, fairness, and consequences, not just capability.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cm">
          <div class="bd"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-eye"/></svg></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Honesty about our tools</h3>
            <p>We practice the transparency we teach. We'll tell you how and where we use AI in this course — and we ask you to do the same. See the charter below.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

