<main>
  <!-- COVER -->
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="topmatter reveal">Course guide · Spring term</p>
      <span class="spine reveal d1">LT · 2010</span>
      <h1 class="reveal d1">Computer Skills <em>for the</em> Information Age</h1>
      <div class="mast-rule reveal d2"></div>
      <p class="lede reveal d2">
        A field guide to learning, working, and creating well in a digital &amp; AI age —
        for students of <strong>every background</strong>, with <strong>no experience required</strong>.
      </p>
      <p class="record reveal d3">
        No prerequisites <span class="sep">/</span> Open to all backgrounds <span class="sep">/</span>
        Spring term <span class="sep">/</span> 11 weeks + break <span class="sep">/</span> 3 assignments
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions reveal d4">
        <a class="btn" href="#schedule">Open the schedule<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <span class="cue">Start in Week 1 with a short AI &amp; digital-tool survey.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 00 OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="entry" id="overview">
    <div class="wrap entry-grid">
      <div class="gutter"><span class="idx">00</span><span class="glabel">Overview</span></div>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <h2>An orientation for a digital &amp; AI age</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            This course helps you become a thoughtful, capable, and ethical participant in a world reshaped by
            computing and artificial intelligence. You'll use computing to <strong>work and create with data</strong>;
            learn effectively <strong>with and without AI</strong>; <strong>find and judge digital information</strong>;
            reason about the <strong>ethics of technology</strong>; and build a <strong>professional digital presence</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            It's designed for students of every background — whether you arrive as a confident coder or have never
            opened a spreadsheet, you'll leave with practical skills and the judgment to use them well.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="facts">
          <li><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-learn"/></svg><span><b>A weekly rhythm.</b> One topic and one discussion each week — a steady, predictable cadence.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-compass"/></svg><span><b>Truly no prerequisites.</b> Nothing here assumes prior coding or technical background.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-design"/></svg><span><b>Learn by doing.</b> Three applied assignments turn ideas into things you've actually made.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-break"/></svg><span><b>Breathing room.</b> The final units span two weeks each so you can finish the term strong.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 01 LEARNING GOALS -->
  <section class="entry" id="goals">
    <div class="wrap entry-grid">
      <div class="gutter"><span class="idx">01</span><span class="glabel">Learning<br>goals</span></div>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <h2>Six skills you'll carry forward</h2>
        <p class="lead">The whole course indexes back to these six capabilities.</p>
        <ul class="index">
          <li>
            <span class="iconbox"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-data"/></svg></span>
            <div><h3>Work with data</h3><p>Use computing to gather, shape, and create with data — the raw material of modern work.</p></div>
            <span class="tag">Data</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="iconbox"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-learn"/></svg></span>
            <div><h3>Learn how to learn</h3><p>Build durable strategies for learning effectively, both with AI and on your own.</p></div>
            <span class="tag">Learning</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="iconbox"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-info"/></svg></span>
            <div><h3>Judge information</h3><p>Find, evaluate, and decide what to trust across a noisy digital landscape.</p></div>
            <span class="tag">Information</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="iconbox"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-ai"/></svg></span>
            <div><h3>Understand AI</h3><p>Develop a working literacy for what AI can and can't do — and how to use it responsibly.</p></div>
            <span class="tag">AI</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="iconbox"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-ethics"/></svg></span>
            <div><h3>Reason about ethics</h3><p>Think critically about the ethics, privacy, and power dynamics technology sets in motion.</p></div>
            <span class="tag">Ethics</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="iconbox"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ic-identity"/></svg></span>
            <div><h3>Present yourself</h3><p>Create a professional digital presence and identity that serves your goals and career.</p></div>
            <span class="tag">Identity</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUTCOMES INTERSTITIAL -->
  <section class="band" id="outcomes" aria-labelledby="outcomes-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="klabel">In your words</p>
      <h2 id="outcomes-h">By the end, I can —</h2>
      <ul class="says">
        <li>find information and explain <em>why</em> I trust it.</li>
        <li>use AI as a tool — and know when <em>not</em> to.</li>
        <li>turn raw data into a story people understand.</li>
        <li>present a professional version of myself online.</li>
        <li>pick up a new tool without being intimidated by it.</li>
        <li>weigh the ethics of a technology before I adopt it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 SCHEDULE -->
  <section class="entry" id="schedule">
    <div class="wrap entry-grid">
      <div class="gutter"><span class="idx">02</span><span class="glabel">Schedule</span></div>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <h2>The arc of the term</h2>
        <p class="lead">Three movements across eleven weeks — foundations, then literacies and ethics, then identity, data, and making.</p>

        <div class="arc-scroll">
          <svg class="arc" viewBox="0 0 1000 200" role="img" aria-label="Timeline across eleven weeks showing three phases and where the three assignments fall.">
